I am not sure why the log cut off before the useful part, but I was able to track it down:

* installing *source* package ‘aquatools’ ...
** R
** data
*** moving datasets to lazyload DB
** inst
** preparing package for lazy loading
Warning: replacing previous import ‘car::recode’ by ‘dplyr::recode’ when loading ‘aquatools’
Warning: replacing previous import ‘dplyr::intersect’ by ‘lubridate::intersect’ when loading ‘aquatools’
Warning: replacing previous import ‘dplyr::union’ by ‘lubridate::union’ when loading ‘aquatools’
Warning: replacing previous import ‘dplyr::setdiff’ by ‘lubridate::setdiff’ when loading ‘aquatools’
Error in loadNamespace(i, c(lib.loc, .libPaths()), versionCheck = vI[[i]]) :
  there is no package called ‘rvest’
ERROR: lazy loading failed for package ‘aquatools’
* removing ‘/usr/local/lib/R/site-library/aquatools’

Looks like you have a dependency upon rvest that isn't declared in your DESCRIPTION file.

